FINDINGS AND OPEN ITEMS
RESOLVED [Q] Registry: default op selection is the UNION of QLinearOpsRegistry,
QDQRegistry and NPUCnnRegistry (quantizers/interface.py:202-227), not NPUCnnRegistry
alone. The exact keys are printed below. Dispatch prioritizes NPUCnnRegistry then
QDQRegistry, then QDQOperatorBase (quantizers/registry.py:145-151).
RESOLVED [Q] Annotation: quantization/quant_utils.py:102 lists Conv, Add, MaxPool,
AveragePool, GlobalAveragePool, MatMul, Gemm, ConvTranspose. Removal also depends on
single-consumer topology, supported downstream activation, and Pad->average-pool
(quant_utils.py:685-736); it is not an unrestricted Conv/Relu rewrite.
RESOLVED [Q] Sharing: extended_quantizer.py:478-509 reuses the upstream provider's
scale and zero-point initializer NAMES for a marked activation. It waits until the
provider is quantized, selects get_for_consumer(node_name), and rejects initializer
sharing. The finite default op list does not imply all inputs of every op quantize:
individual ORT handlers decide slots, exclusions, and sharing. Detailed handler
eligibility beyond the Phase 1 ResNet graph remains OPEN for Phase 2 transcription.
RESOLVED [Q] Bias: npu_cnn_quantizer.py:200-216 calls quantize_weight_tensor for
default int8 bias. Therefore initial bias position uses its own MinMSE values,
not ipos+wpos; qdq_quantizer.py:931-956 -> quant_utils.py:1089-1118.
RESOLVED [Q] Rounding/storage: quant_utils.py:527-535 casts inputs to float32,
divides by scale, numpy .round() (ties to even), adds zero point, and clips using
symmetric=True. INT8 storage clips to [-127,127], NOT the full [-128,127] range
(quant_utils.py:364-379,474-486). UINT8 clips to [0,255]. Weight/activation arithmetic
differs from the EP's rounding setting; this audit makes no NPU rounding claim.
RESOLVED [Q] MinMSE: quant_utils.py:1089-1118 searches base_pos-1 through base_pos+3,
with strict '<' selecting the first minimum. float16 activation storage is converted
back to float32 for this computation (calibrators.py:675-695; collectors.py:337-350).
scale2pos clamps scale into [2^-127,2^127] before rint(-log2(scale)) (:814-833).
RESOLVED [Q] Refine dispatch/directions, postprocess/refinement/refine.py:
  shift_cut :164-203 applies ONLY Conv/Gemm; wpos = clamp(sc,0,16)+opos-ipos.
  shift_bias :205-254 applies ONLY Conv/Gemm; bpos = wpos+ipos-clamp(sb,min_sb,15);
    min_sb=min(0,shift_cut-16), except direct LeakyRelu successor forces 0.
  shift_read :380-427 applies Add/Sub; lowers ONE argmax input to min(ipos)+7 per pass.
  shift_write :430-543 applies Add/Mul; moves output to min(ipos)-clamp(sw,-7,25)
    or sum(ipos)-clamp(sw,0,32), respectively.
  HardSigmoid :330-377 clamps ipos to [0,15], then opos to [7,14+new_ipos].
  Swish :256-324 moves opos = ipos0+ipos1-clamp(shift_swish,0,15); source matcher
    recognizes a Mul input also consumed by a qualifying HardSigmoid.
  Concat :545-583 assigns ALL available input and output positions their minimum.
  Pool :585-610 aligns MaxPool/AveragePool/GlobalAveragePool to min(ipos,opos).
  Pad :613-639 and Slice :641-666 likewise choose the minimum on both sides.
  Resize is NOT covered by this manager's alignment rules (handler sharing is separate).
  Rule order :686-724: concat,pool,pad,slice,read,write,cut,bias,hard_sigmoid,swish.
CORRECTION: draft DESIGN.md confused QuantPosManager (XINT8 adjust_quantize_info)
with QuantInfoManager (general align_quantize_info). Output-led concat alignment
and unconditional input-led pool alignment described the latter, not this path.
OPEN [U] Refine implementation hazards: Mul shift_write omits has_change=True
(:537-539); set_scale's raw_data branch assigns to a temporary list (:49-57).
Need focused Phase 1 comparison before deciding bug compatibility. No edited vendor
code and no claim these branches affect the inspected models. Refine only changes
scale metadata, not initializer integer values; Phase 1 must account for any
post-rounding scale moves when matching weights from an original float graph.
RESOLVED [Q][M] HardSigmoid beta: omitted by converter (:86-98); default beta=0.5
in the installed ONNX opset-17 schema. quant_utils.py:622-632 accepts absence or
approximately 0.5; fingerprint prints actual model attributes.
RESOLVED [Q] CLE defaults: algorithm/interface.py:61-66: steps=1, balance=max,
weight_threshold=0.5, append_bias=True, use_threshold=True, total_diff_threshold=2e-7.
RESOLVED [Q] Large pool: optimizations/optimize.py:190-250 only splits a rank-4
GlobalAveragePool with spatial area >512, once. Near-square integer factors must
leave both resulting areas <=512, otherwise skip. Prepending AveragePool uses its
kernel dimensions as strides, while the original GlobalAveragePool remains.
RESOLVED [Q] Simulation defaults: npu_cnn_quantizer.py:293-324 explicitly enables
LeakyRelu, Sigmoid, HardSigmoid, AvgPool, ReduceMean; disables Softmax,
InstanceNormalization, Clip. The wrapper's own all-True defaults are not this path.
  LeakyRelu alpha rounds to multiples of 1/256 (:70-84).
  ReduceMean multiplies by a shape/axes-dependent nearest dyadic reciprocal
    correction (:185-242); behavior is now sourced, no implementation yet.
  Optional Softmax delegates to SimulateDPUSoftmax (:261-274). Its full expansion
    remains OPEN (Phase 2 only if enabled/encountered); default XINT8 disables it.
  Optional InstanceNorm becomes a custom-domain operator, preserving epsilon
    (:276-295); optional Clip rounds/clamps initializer limits to [-128,127]
    (:297-345). No acceptance claim for either disabled rewrite.
RESOLVED [Q] Calibration reader: calibration/data_readers.py:544-579 returns the
provided object without an isinstance test; calibrators.py:679 calls get_next().
Quark imports ORT's CalibrationDataReader, not a distinct Quark base class.
Reader methods needed by calibration/CLE/finetune should still be supplied by the
comparison adapter; no Quark import is necessary in quant/.
RESOLVED [Q] XINT8_ADAROUND preset: custom_config.py:20-30 has DataSize=1000,
FixedSeed=1705472343, BatchSize=2, NumIterations=1000, LearningRate=0.1,
OptimAlgorithm=adaround, OptimDevice=cpu, InferDevice=cpu, EarlyStop=True.
RESOLVED [Q] AdaRound core schedule: train_model_param.py:24-48 gives reg=0.01,
beta=(20,2), warm_start=0.2; train_model_loss.py:44-79 uses zero rounding penalty
until warmup ends and cosine beta decay thereafter. base_qdq_quantizers.py:192-263
uses gamma=-0.1,zeta=1.1 and floor+clamped stretched sigmoid; hard result alpha>=0.
train_model.py:55-158 uses Adam on alpha, random batch permutations, quantized
inputs at default drop_ratio=1, and immediate early stop when the rolling rounding
loss fails to improve. Full layer caching/selection and selective-update handling
remain OPEN for Phase 3; schedule alone does not establish AdaRound parity.
OPEN [U] Consumer metadata: producer_name, metadata_props, and opset-import
sensitivity cannot be established by reading producer source or vaip_config.json.
Needs Phase 4 one-variable EP probes, including SAME-model CPU/NPU output checks.
OPEN [U] Phase 1 exact re-emission: no fresh no-CLE Quark reference run yet, no
graph_diff, no full-set CPU evaluation and no EP engagement/latency gates attempted.
Existing resnet50_xint8_c64 is fingerprint evidence only, not a Phase 1 oracle.

